  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `xtask/src/quick_subs.rs`: these items in a submodule count as shared, so the whole suite runs:\n  - `impl <Trait> for <Type>` (also generic and `unsafe impl`);\n  - `pub` after attributes on the same line (`#[allow(dead_code)] pub fn`);\n  - `pub(crate)`, `pub(super)`, `pub(in ..)`.\n\n  An inherent `impl Type { .. }` of a private type keeps the `<sub>::` filter.\n- `xtask/src/braces.rs` (`code`):\n  - `cr\"..\"` and `cr#\"..\"#` are raw strings now. Before, `cr\"a \\\"` read the rest of the line as a string.\n  - An escaped char literal (`'\\''`, `'\\'`) ends at its last quote.\n- `xtask/src/scan.rs` (`test_fns`): the new pins found two defects that were already on main.\n  - A `#[test]` below a line like `#[allow(dead_code)] pub fn helper() {}` made `test_fns` loop forever, with no limit on the memory. The attribute walk took the fn line, and the loop did not move on. Now the walk stops at a line that holds a fn, and the loop always moves on. A quick plan of such a file hung the gate.\n  - `fn_re` did not read `pub(crate) fn` or the `const` / `unsafe` / `extern \"C\"` qualifiers. Such a line was read as an attribute of the next test, so an edit there ran only that test.\n- `xtask/src/directory_tests.rs`: `run_step` returns libtest's stdout.\n- `xtask/src/directory_edges_tests.rs`: the loop variable `whole` is now `outside_fns`.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/3711-quick-subs-guards.md`.\n\n## Readings (base origin/main `d54580cad`, head after the merge of main)\n\n| Plan | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`, all steps | 1297 | 1297 |\n| the same, heavy steps | 101 | 101 (the same list, checked with `diff`) |\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run` | 1 (xtask unit tests) | 1 |\n| `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run` | 0 | 0 |\n\nNote: the base has 101 heavy steps, not 99. Main has moved since PR #3709. This PR does not change the heavy plan.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `directory_tests::selection::a_trait_impl_or_a_scoped_pub_in_a_submodule_runs_the_whole_suite` (8 cases)\n- `directory_tests::selection::an_inherent_impl_of_a_private_type_keeps_the_submodule_filter`\n- `directory_tests::selection::a_submodule_step_runs_only_that_submodule_in_real_cargo`: a real `cargo test --test many -- --test-threads=6 alpha::` on a fixture crate. It reads `1 passed` and `4 filtered out` (top, beta, shared, gated). The fixture run takes less than 1 min.\n- `braces::tests::a_mod_token_in_a_literal_or_comment_is_blanked_and_the_real_one_stays` (16 rows: `\"...\"`, `\\\"`, `r\"..\"`, `r#\"..\"#`, `br\"..\"`, `b\"..\"`, `cr\"..\"`, `cr#\"..\"#`, `c\"..\"`, nested block comments, `'\"'`, `'\\''`, `'\\'`, `b'\"'`, lifetimes, `//` comment)\n- `braces::tests::a_block_comment_and_a_string_carry_over_to_the_next_line`\n- `braces::tests::a_test_after_an_attributed_fn_on_one_line_is_found_and_the_scan_ends` (the loop defect and the `pub(crate)` / `const unsafe` fn lines)\n\nRed first: the trait-impl pin hung on the old code (the `scan::test_fns` loop, found in the first run). On the old code, the `pub(crate)` case planned `--exact alpha::a1`. A full red-first run of all pins on the old code was not done.\n\n## Quick gate (final head, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`)\n\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p xtask -- --test-threads=6`: 322 unit tests and all integration binaries pass.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real cut gate.\n- A full red-first run of each pin on the old code.\n\nEffort: medium (not escalated).\n\nChangelog: none\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #3711\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
